{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b7d5245f-77ce-48c1-8f3f-a89a5e1f4f71","agentId":"a7730a69efb7861a9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no web searching, no screenshots (memory is low). Token-efficient: read only the functions you change; 3 checks; report under 80 words. Files only: mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py (depends_on edges and a new per-system `technical` dict), cuore/web/systems_routes.py, cuore/web/templates/systems.html, cuore/web/systems_svg.py (edge/node <title> and detail ids only), mes-log-mcp/tests/check_systems.py (+3 checks). House rules: every value cites a source and confidence; UNKNOWN with \"see the wiring diagrams / service manual (TechAuthority)\"; never invent pin numbers, voltages or limits. Existing sourced facts to reuse (read only those entries): mes/electrical.py (F82, BCM feeds, XY201, G003A/B, ESIM connector, module locations), mes/layout_systems.py (components and locations), cuore/live/buses.py (CAN-C 500 kbit/s pins 6/14; CAN-IHS 125 kbit/s; CAN-CH reachability), mes/known_good.py (bands), mes/knowledge.py (TSB texts incl. voltage-drop and ground checks), cuore/live/did_catalog.py (DIDs per module), mes/parts.py.\n\nEnrich: (1) each depends_on edge gains `technical`: {carries: \"12 V supply\"|\"ground\"|\"CAN data\"|\"vacuum\"|\"pressure\"|\"coolant flow\"|\"oil pressure\"|..., path: [element ids from electrical/layout where known], bus: {name, speed} for data links, measure: {what, where (element id), limit, source, confidence} (e.g. voltage drop across a ground strap: limit only if the TSB states one; else UNKNOWN), propagates: plain sentence of the failure mode (e.g. \"low supply voltage at the BCM makes several modules drop off CAN: U-codes on many modules at once\"), tsb_refs}. (2) each SYSTEM gains `technical`: {modules: [codes with bus], dids: [first 8 catalogued DID names], live_channels_with_bands: [{channel, normal, warn, confidence}], components: [{id, label, zone}], codes_owned: [exact codes from CODE_RULES]}. (3) Systems page: tapping a node or an edge opens a detail block (plain <details> with ids `node-<key>` and `edge-<a>-<b>`; the SVG elements link to them with <a href=\"#...\">) showing those facts in compact tables with confidence chips; the edge's measure line reads e.g. \"Measure: voltage drop G003A to battery negative, limit UNKNOWN (TechAuthority), source S2008000032\". Checks: every edge has a technical dict with carries and propagates; at least 3 edges have a sourced measure; the Systems page renders an edge detail for network->electrical_supply containing \"Measure\". Run check_systems.py and cuore/tests/check_systems_page.py (TestClient portion only if the CDP part can be skipped via an env flag; otherwise run check_systems_api.py instead)."},"uuid":"f6064efa-35fa-4f50-b843-8b7db2f04c1e","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:45:13.538Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
